    "created_at": "2022-06-08T15:15:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-08T15:15:24Z",
    "body": "I doubt we are using it consistently. But the algorithms in https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#strings use it indirectly quite a lot, e.g. \"Let potentialPrefixCodeUnit be the ith [code unit](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit) of potentialPrefix.\" where i can be 0. And the plus side is that nobody will be confused by 0th, although they might be confused by first.\r\n\r\nAllowing string[0] is a bit tricky IMO because it doesn't clarify whether that's code point or code unit. Maybe <var>string</var>[0]<sub>cu</sub> and <var>string</var>[0]<sub>cp</sub>, but that feels a bit like adding notation for notation's sake...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
